1. 搜尋頁面 (EastSun: "我在頁面這邊需要一個可以搜尋關鍵字的輸入點")
A webview view right above the 頁面 list (a tree view cannot hold an input),
like the box on top of Visual Studio's Solution Explorer. Typing filters the
list: pages whose name / title has every word, the components that have them
(name, class, text; highlighted, a click opens the page and selects it), and
pages whose shown text has them (a tab label has no id). Enter: an exact
component name, else a page by its name, else the best component; Esc
clears; Down goes into the list; Ctrl+F in the list comes back. The page
parse is cached by mtime (first search ~120 ms, then ~15 ms).
<style id> / <script id> are no longer "components" in the search.

2. 機種與機台設定, read only (EastSun: "這IO頁面 怎感覺有缺? ... 少了這個" --
the Above9050 tab of HW.IoSetView)
Those pages ask wb_serve (GET /api/system/gerneral) and take the machine from
the launch URL (background.html?machine=HT9050); the designer has no network,
so they showed their "no server" face. Now the designer takes both from what
F5 starts wb_serve with (.vscode/launch.json: W906_HMI_URL's machine=,
W906_GENERAL_INI_PATH, W906_AUTH_PATH\config.ini): lib/liveconfig.js reads
the ini files (never writes) into wb_serve's shape (RecipeDocToJson rules:
first section / key wins, BCB6 trim + one quote pair, int / float / string);
the probe puts the machine in the launch options and answers only those
GETs; every other connection is still blocked. A page that picks its JSON
folder by its address (/page/ -> ../JSON/) gets the web root's.
右鍵「顯示」->「設計檢視的機種…」: like F5 / HT9045 / HT9050 / none; the
status bar says it. Settings generalIni / configIni can point elsewhere.

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 142, smoke 144, real VS Code 135): lib (filterPages, highlights, launchHints, iniToDoc incl. Big5 and
repeated sections), probe (the real HW.IoSetView in headless Edge: HT9050,
Above9050 opened, gerneral + config answered, View-rules.json moved; without:
the old face), smoke (the box, the list, Enter, clear, the machine pick and
what the page gets), real VS Code (grpLoader_9050 found, opened from the list,
visible for HT9050, hidden with none).

